────────────────────
+ do paint
    - canvas Canvas

//+tui.frame.animation
. should-flush-animation = did-initial-layout
if should-flush-animation
    flush-animation-frames-before-paint()
//-tui.frame.animation

` Root-controlled phase order: checkpoint the batch so phases observe stable computed style, then
` run layout top-down before painting. A clean queue, a clean store, and a clean tree all exit
` immediately, so no pending-check is needed here; the layout walk arranges only raised subtrees
` and clears each bit as the work completes.
//+tui.frame.markup-checkpoint
catch markup-batch-queue.checkpoint()
//-tui.frame.markup-checkpoint
settle-pending-focus()
catch validate-focus()
//+tui.frame.layout
update-layout()
//-tui.frame.layout
if !should-flush-animation && animation-frame-callbacks
    flush-initial-animation-frames-before-paint()
did-initial-layout = true
reveal-pending-focus()

//+tui.frame.paint-tree
compositor.paint(this, canvas)
//-tui.frame.paint-tree

did-paint()

if !should-flush-animation && animation-frame-callbacks
    (catch? terminal)?.schedule-animation-frame()

= focused-paint-result()

────────────────────
+ do markup-batch-did-flush
    - flush MarkupBatchFlush

` The window is the root phase controller: settling raised persistent domain bits on the nodes
` whose declared properties changed. Pending layout or paint state schedules a paint; the paint
` pass runs layout top-down first when any layout is pending, and each phase clears its bits as
` the work completes.
if flush.is-layout-invalid || flush.is-paint-invalid
    catch schedule-paint()
refresh-modal-box()
settle-pending-focus()

